		<div class="texto-blog">					
		<p>In this article we will see <strong>CodeIgniter 4 Forms</strong>, with the use of the security class, we will use the command line tool and route handling.</p>

		<h2>How to create Forms in Codeigniter 4?</h2>

		{{ include('inc/ad_defect.html.twig') }} 	
		
		<p>First it is necessary to create a controller, we will enter the following command, if you do not know the basics of this framework read the following article <a class="text-info" href="/codeigniter-4-tutorial">CodeIgniter 4 Tutorial</a>.</p>

		<code>php spark make:controller Persons</code>

		<p>Which will create the base structure of a controller in codeigniter 4, we will work with a controller called Persons.</p>

		<div class="text-center">

		<img class="img-fluid" src="../assets/img/ci4_form1.png" alt="ci4_rutasapi">

		</div>

		<p>We will add the following code inside the controller.</p>

		<pre class="text-code">
		<code>
		namespace App\Controllers;

		use App\Controllers\BaseController;

		class Persons extends BaseController
		{

			public function __construct()
			{		
				helper('form');
			}

			public function index()
			{
				return view('persons');
			}

			public function create()
			{
				$email = $this->request->getPost('email');
				$password = $this->request->getPost('password');

				dd($email.$password);
			}

		}
		</code>
		</pre>

		<p>We will create a new view in <code>nameProject/app/Views/persons.php</code> and we will add the following method <code>return view('persons');</code>, where we will pass the people view as a parameter to the view method, we create a constructor where we will load the <code>helper('form');</code>.</p>

		<p>We create the set of necessary routes of type get and post.</p>

		<code>
		$routes->get('/persons', 'Persons::index');		
		</code>
		<br>
		<code>
		$routes->post('/persons', 'Persons::create');
		</code>

		<p>We verify the set of routes.</p>

		<code>
		php spark routes
		</code>

		<div class="text-center">

		<img class="img-fluid" src="../assets/img/ci4_form2.png" alt="ci4_rutasapi">

		</div>

		<p>We will go to the browser to show the view.</p>

		<div class="text-center">

		<img class="img-fluid" src="../assets/img/ci4_form3.png" alt="ci4_rutasapi">

		</div>

		<p>In the persons view we create the following form, we will use 2 methods for CSRF protection.</p>

		<div class="text-center">

		<img class="img-fluid" src="../assets/img/ci4_form4.png" alt="ci4_rutasapi">

		</div>

		<p>We will enable CSRF protection in the .env file.</p>		

		<pre class="text-code">
		<code>
		#--------------------------------------------------------------------
		# SECURITY
		#--------------------------------------------------------------------

		  security.tokenName = 'csrf_token_name'
		  security.headerName = 'X-CSRF-TOKEN'
		  security.cookieName = 'csrf_cookie_name'
		  security.expires = 7200
		  security.regenerate = true
		  security.redirect = true
		  security.samesite = 'Lax'
		</code>
		</pre>

		<p>We send a post type request and show the result.</p>

